                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "20839945",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197981187749",
                            "num_reviews": 22,
                            "playtime_forever": 215,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 209,
                            "last_played": 1455825130
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Usually not a fan of Early Access games, but for this developer I make an exception!\n\nThe daily streams on twitch are a great way to see progress being made and provide the peace of mind that the project isn't going to have a year long hiatus without any news or updates.\n\nThe game itself:\nA callback to classic gaming with a gorgeous artstyle and mixing in some new mechanics! There is a lot of potential here and I'm really excited to play the entire game. \n\nYes, it is early access, so there are still some bugs here and there, but it's a very playable game right now and I haven't run into any game breaking issues yet which is pretty impressive for a game that was just launched. \n\nThe crafting system has some interesting choices on how much it impacts the gameplay. You really start to feel mighty after leveling up your stats a couple of times. So, don't despair if you start off having a hard time taking on the imaginary monsters in the world! \n\nThere are also many secrets hidden around the world and they are a lot of fun to find!\n\nTLDR: Buy this game if you like classic Zelda gameplay and exploration and want to support a dedicated developer",
